**Producer:** {{producer_name}} ({{producer_alias}}), {{producer_email}}

**Artist:** {{artist_name}} ({{artist_alias}}), {{artist_email}}

Date: {{agreement_date}}. Beat: "{{beat_title}}" (the "Beat"). New song: "{{song_title}}" (the "New Song"). Every recorded song has two separate copyrights: the composition (music and lyrics), usually owned by songwriters and their publishers, and the sound recording or master, usually owned by whoever paid for or made the recording (the artist or label). Licenses and splits for one do not cover the other.

This license covers up to:
- {{stream_cap}} audio streams in total across all platforms;
- {{sales_cap}} downloads and physical units in total;
- {{video_cap}} music video(s), with up to {{video_views_cap}} total views across video platforms.

Once Artist reaches any limit, or the term ends, Artist must stop new exploitation of the New Song or obtain a new license or upgrade. Copies already sold and existing streams are not recalled. Artist: [[initial:artist]]
